# Exact printing of money amounts

Money is an exact number of cents; its JSON output must not go through a
binary float, which resolves cents only below 2^46 units.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope Amounts:
  output beyond_float content money
  output division content money
  output negative_cents content money
  output zero content money

scope Amounts:
  definition beyond_float equals $90,071,992,547,409.93
  definition division equals $99,999,999,999,999,999,999.99 / 3
  definition negative_cents equals $0 - $0.05
  definition zero equals $0
```

```catala-test-cli
$ catala test-scope Amounts -F json
{"beyond_float":"90071992547409.93","division":"33333333333333333333.33","negative_cents":"-0.05","zero":"0.00"}
```

```catala-test-cli
$ catala test-scope Amounts
┌─[RESULT]─ Amounts ─
│ beyond_float = $90,071,992,547,409.93
│ division = $33,333,333,333,333,333,333.33
│ negative_cents = -$0.05
│ zero = $0.00
└─
```
